 "response": "Kakir's budget is now **$1075K**.\n\n**How I worked it out:**\n\n1. I counted only Finance Office messages, as the policy requires. Notes from PMO, Engineering, Sales, Legal and others don't change the budget. Finance Office entries that aren't budget changes, such as audits, receipts and purchase orders, don't either.\n\n2. I worked out which updates are withdrawn by going backwards from the latest withdrawal. A withdrawal counts only if no later withdrawal cancels it. Some chains go several levels deep:\n   - **#1598 \u2192 #1092 \u2192 #1041:** #1092 is cancelled, so the +$593K in #1041 stands.\n   - **#1039 \u2192 #1023 \u2192 #0956 \u2192 #0711 \u2192 #0111 \u2192 #0007 \u2192 #0003:** #0007 is cancelled, so the \u2212$11K in #0003 stands.\n   - **#0835 \u2192 #0829 \u2192 #0034 \u2192 #0030:** #0034 stays in force, so the +$482K in #0030 stays withdrawn.\n\n   Altogether about 150 budget updates end up withdrawn.\n\n3. I started from $1280K, set in #0001. I then applied every remaining increase and decrease in record order. The running total ends at $1075K after the last change, #1599 (\u2212$75K).\n\nANSWER: $1075K",
